cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyinterp, please cite it using the metadata of this file."
type: software
title: "pyinterp: fast interpolation of geo-referenced data"
abstract: >-
  pyinterp is a Python library, written in C++, for the interpolation of
  geo-referenced data: gridded fields in 2, 3 or 4 dimensions, with periodic
  longitudes and temporal axes, and scattered observations indexed in
  R*-trees. It also provides gap filling, binning and streaming statistics,
  and geometric algorithms in Cartesian and geographic coordinates.
authors:
  - family-names: Briol
    given-names: Frédéric
  - name: CNES
  - name: CLS
repository-code: "https://github.com/CNES/pangeo-pyinterp"
url: "https://cnes.github.io/pangeo-pyinterp/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - interpolation
  - xarray
  - geospatial
  - geodesy
  - oceanography
  - climate
  - satellite
  - rtree
